          <p>Buenas d&iacute;as amigos y familia!<br><br>
          This week has been rough, not gonna lie. I've been frustrated and bored and wishing I was home. I told my president that I was thinking about going home but all the temples are closed so I guess I'll stay here lol.<br><br>
          Biggest news is that I transferred last night! I am now in the Friendswood zone and the Manvel Area. My new companion is Hermana Crookston. She seems really nice! She is from Virginia and goes to school at BYU. She has a boyfriend that she already has a date to marry. She only has 3 or 4 transfers left.<br><br>
          We still are staying inside the apartment all day. There are no signs of anything changing anytime soon. The peak of COVID should be this week in Houston.<br><br>
          My companions and I went on a couple bike rides on trails by the bayou and it was really pretty. I really appreciated the chance to be outside in nature and the air felt so fresh!<br><br>
          It was sad to leave Hermana Rich and Hermana house and the cute people we were teaching. I will especially miss sweet Yancy and sweet Maria. I hope that I will make it back to H8 someday so I can actually meet them in person. On my last day in the area we finally had a lesson with the family that we have a few of them on date to be baptized! Cute family. Hopefully they go through with their baptisms and can be baptized soon. And I had to pack up everything again. Hermana Crookston is my 5th companion and it's only my 41st day on the mission!<br><br>
          The weather here has been really nice this week. There was a tornado warning yesterday but that didn't happen. The rain and thunderstorms are really cool here.<br><br>
          How are you all? How are your families? What's the big news? Miss you and love you all.<br><br>
          Les amo<br><br><br>
          Hermana Barton</p>
